        {
          "id": "hook",
          "type": "PROBLEM",
          "enabled": true,
          "narration": "A message lands at ten at night. \"How much for bridal makeup?\" You reply: ₦45,000. Two minutes later: \"Last price, dear?\" Then someone else asks the same thing. By morning you have quoted three different prices, and you cannot remember who got which. So how do you stop haggling in your DMs without losing the client?",
          "estimatedDurationSeconds": 23.3,
          "visualInstructions": "A phone at night: an Instagram DM thread. \"How much for bridal makeup?\", the reply \"₦45,000\", then \"Last price, dear?\". A second and third thread with the same question. All names fictional.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "story",
            "mode": "problem",
            "lines": [
              {
                "text": "What happens",
                "role": "lead"
              },
              {
                "text": "Why it matters",
                "role": "key"
              }
            ],
            "recede": true,
            "settled": []
          },
          "animation": {
            "enter": "rise",
            "leadInSeconds": 0.4,
            "tailSeconds": 0.5,
            "minDurationSeconds": 0
