        {
          "id": "gap",
          "type": "EXPLANATION",
          "enabled": true,
          "narration": "Haggling starts because your price lives in your head, not where the client can see it. Every chat starts from zero, so the client tests the number. When you are tired, or a slot is empty, you drop it. The client who pushed hardest pays the least. The loyal one who never asked pays full price.",
          "estimatedDurationSeconds": 23.3,
          "visualInstructions": "The price as a thought bubble over the owner, not written anywhere. Three chats, three different numbers.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "comparison",
            "left": {
              "title": "The usual way",
              "points": [
                "First point"
              ],
              "tone": "neutral"
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "A better way",
              "points": [
                "First point"
              ],
              "tone": "neutral"
            }
          },
          "animation": {
            "enter": "rise",
            "leadInSeconds": 0.4,
            "tailSeconds": 0.5,
            "minDurationSeconds": 0
          },
          "captions": {
            "enabled": true
          },
          "audio": {
            "narrationVolume": 1
          },
          "chapterTitle": "Why it breaks",
          "assets": []
        },
        {
          "id": "how-it-works",
          "type": "DIAGRAM",
          "enabled": true,
          "narration": "This fix works with or without software. Write down every service, its price and what it includes. Put that list where clients see it before they message you. And decide your discounts in advance, not in the middle of a chat. You still set every price. You just stop renegotiating it one DM at a time.",
          "estimatedDurationSeconds": 23.3,
          "visualInstructions": "Three steps: 1. Write every price down. 2. Show it before the chat. 3. Decide discounts in advance. The owner stays in charge of every number.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "pipeline",
            "object": {
              "type": "transaction",
              "label": "Payment"
            },
            "stages": [
              {
                "label": "First step",
                "status": "verified"
              },
              {
                "label": "Second step",
                "status": "verified"
              },
              {
                "label": "Third step",
                "status": "verified"
              }
            ],
            "settled": []
          },
          "animation": {
            "enter": "rise",
            "leadInSeconds": 0.4,
            "tailSeconds": 0.5,
            "minDurationSeconds": 0
          },
          "captions": {
            "enabled": true
          },
          "audio": {
            "narrationVolume": 1
          },
          "chapterTitle": "A better way",
          "assets": []
        },
        {
          "id": "product-intro",
          "type": "DEMO",
          "enabled": true,
          "narration": "In Iker, that list is your Rate card. Each service has a name, a price, a duration, and what is included and what is not. The business on screen is made up, with demo data.",
          "estimatedDurationSeconds": 14.9,
          "visualInstructions": "Dashboard sidebar, \"Rate card\" highlighted, then the services list. Point at price, duration, included and excluded items. Demo data, labelled.",
          "visual": {
            "kind": "product",
